# The scenario Lambda's image (services/scenario/Dockerfile) builds with
# the repo root as context -- needed so it can also COPY services/tiles
# (a sibling package, see that Dockerfile's own comment on why). Without
# this file, `docker build` would try to send the *entire* repo as build
# context first, including data/ and apps/web/public/data (symlinks to the
# main worktree's multi-GB pipeline outputs, see bin/link-data) -- slow at
# best, likely to fail outright at that size. Only services/scenario/ and
# services/tiles/ are ever actually COPY'd, so everything else is safe to
# exclude here regardless of what a future Dockerfile might add, as long
# as it's kept in sync with what it COPYs.
data/
apps/web/public/data/
apps/web/node_modules/
apps/web/dist/
.git/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
infra/cdk.out/
